# HOLOS service configuration.
#
# The server itself takes flags, not environment variables. This file is the configuration
# layer: run.sh and run.ps1 read it and translate it into flags. Keeping it this way means
# the binary stays inspectable — `holos-server --help` is the whole surface — while
# deployments still get one file to edit and one file to put under version control.
#
# Copy to holos.env.local (git-ignored) and edit that, or set these in the environment.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- network --
# Bind address. Keep this on loopback in any deployment that has a front door;
# the front door is what listens on a public interface. See OPERATIONS.md.
HOLOS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:7878

# Worker threads. One request occupies one thread for its whole life, so this is the
# ceiling on concurrent queries, not a pool over an async runtime. 8 is the default.
HOLOS_THREADS=8

# Serve the YASGUI console at /. Turn it off for a machine-to-machine endpoint: with
# --no-ui the process needs no outbound network access of any kind.
HOLOS_UI=on

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ data ---
# Persistent RocksDB store directory. Leave empty for an in-memory store that is
# discarded on exit. Exactly one process may hold this directory at a time.
HOLOS_STORE=./var/store

# Files to load at every start-up, space-separated. Loading is idempotent, so a restart
# does not duplicate anything — but it re-parses every file every time. Prefer loading
# once with deploy/load.sh and leaving this empty. Useful for read-only demo instances.
HOLOS_DATA=

# ------------------------------------------------------------- identity ----
# Read the principal from X-Holos-Principal / X-Holos-Roles / X-Holos-Clearance.
#
# ONLY turn this on when a front door sets those headers AND strips whatever the client
# sent. On an open port it lets any caller name its own roles and clearance. Off by
# default, and the server prints a line at start-up saying which way it is running.
HOLOS_TRUST_FORWARDED=off

# Development shortcut: give every request these roles and this clearance, regardless of
# headers. Never set these on a shared or production instance.
HOLOS_DEV_ROLES=
HOLOS_DEV_CLEARANCE=

# ------------------------------------------------------------- policy ------
# Start from deny-by-default instead of permit-all. With this on, nothing is readable
# until an --allow rule grants it.
HOLOS_DENY_ALL=off

# Error on refusal instead of filtering silently. Filtering is the default because it
# gives the query the answer the principal is entitled to; failing is right when a
# partial answer would be misread as a complete one. See OPERATIONS.md.
HOLOS_FAIL_CLOSED=off

# Space-separated IRIs.
HOLOS_ALLOW_GRAPHS=
HOLOS_DENY_PREDICATES=

# Space-separated IRI=LEVEL pairs, e.g.
#   HOLOS_LABEL_GRAPHS="http://example.com/reviews=3 http://example.com/legal=5"
# A principal reads a labelled graph only if its clearance dominates the label.
HOLOS_LABEL_GRAPHS=
